  "airline": "CAY",
  "name": "Coat of arms tail",
  "kind": "standard",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "drawnOn": "B38M",
  "description": "White fuselage with 'Cayman Airways' in navy serif over the forward windows and Sir Turtle, the airline's mascot, just behind the forward door. The fin carries the Cayman Islands' coat of arms: a red chief with a gold lion at the top, then white and blue waves with three green stars edged in gold. At the fin's root the arms' crest (a turtle on a red and gold wreath) sits on the fillet, and a gold scroll with the motto 'HE HATH FOUNDED IT UPON THE SEAS' curves down across the aft fuselage. White engines; winglets in the same arms.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VP-CIZ_@_MIA,_2023-01-17.jpg",
      "title": "VP-CIZ @ MIA, 2023-01-17.jpg (CC BY-SA 2.0, Colin Cooke Photo)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-20",
      "note": "737-8 VP-CIZ landing at Miami, right side, 2023-01-17. Flipped and fitted to shapes/B38M.json (both doors pinned, within 2-17 px): the fin's red chief, waves and stars (columns sampled across the fin), the crest and scroll, the title and mascot."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VP-CIY_@_MIA,_2024-04-01.png",
      "title": "VP-CIY @ MIA, 2024-04-01.png (CC BY-SA 2.0, Mark Bess)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-20",
      "note": "737-8 VP-CIY at Miami, left side from a little above, 2024-04-01. Fitted to shapes/B38M.json (within about 30 px): the left side matches; the motto's run and angle on the scroll; the winglet."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:02142019_Cayman_Airways_B738M_VP-CIW_KMIA_NASEDIT_(47110424502).jpg",
